# hirschgarten (Snowflake fork)

Read these two files at the repository root before proposing any change:

1. **`AGENTS.md`** — canonical agent guidance for this repository. This rule defers to it; do not
   duplicate guidance here.
2. **`CONTEXT_DEVELOPMENT_261.md`** — the branch handoff document for `development-261`: current state,
   recently merged PRs, open items, decisions already taken and reversed, and which source files are
   upstream-maintained versus Snowflake-only.

Each long-lived development branch carries its own `CONTEXT_DEVELOPMENT_<ijVersion>.md`. If the file
named above is absent, look for `CONTEXT_DEVELOPMENT_*.md` at the repository root and read that.

The single rule most often violated by an agent that skipped the above: **rebase cost is not uniform
across this repository.** Some files are Snowflake-only and can be restructured freely; others are
upstream-maintained and actively churned, so edits there must stay additive and small. Prefer a new
Snowflake-owned file in the same package over appending declarations to an upstream file, and prefer
wrapping a call site over re-indenting an upstream function body. See the "Fork Topology" section of
the context document for the table and the commands to re-derive it.
